  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development of economic opportunities, such as ecotourism, as an alternative to unsustainable.agricultural and other destructive practices upon the natural ecosystems in the communities on La.Amistad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support the conservation of the La Amistad International Park in Costa Rica through the development of economic opportunities related to ecotourism in the communities within and adjacent to the park. The project is intended to conserve the largest natural forest of Costa Rica and the rich array of wildlife that is supports including jaguars, pumas, Bairds tapirs, and peccaries by addressing the impacts of poaching, wildlife trafficking, and illegal and unsustainable natural resource extraction. Specific activities include: (1) identify and develop business plans for at least twelve ecotourism related ventures; (2) strengthen local tourism and community associations; (3) deliver training to both community groups as well as to protected area personnel on the benefits and impacts of tourism, including exchanges with successful community-based ecotourism projects in other areas of the country; (4) deliver training on the design, construction and maintenance of trails; and (5) support sales and marketing activities to promote ecotourism in the park.</narrative>
  </description>
